Package: tower
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.9), procps
Recommends: systemd, tmux, python3-gi, python3-gi-cairo, gir1.2-gtk-3.0,
 gir1.2-ayatanaappindicator3-0.1 | gir1.2-appindicator3-0.1
Suggests: nodejs, gnome-shell-extension-appindicator
Homepage: https://github.com/imanimen/tower
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Description: control tower for your Claude Code agents
 Tower pins Claude Code to a country (the fence), isolates network faults
 (the weather), watches plan usage, and monitors every running Claude agent.
 .
 One daemon owns all the logic and state; the front-ends are thin. This package
 has both of them: "tower-tray" puts the radar in your top bar with a panel
 behind it — the counterpart of Tower's macOS menu-bar app — and "tower" is the
 curses terminal dashboard, which needs no graphical session at all.
 .
 The guard is fail-closed: a Claude request is allowed only when Tower has
 *confirmed* you are inside the target country and that there is a usable
 network path to Anthropic. Anything uncertain is held and answered 503, which
 Claude Code shows as its own "Retrying" spinner, so a blocked request is
 pending rather than failed and resumes on its own.
 .
 Routing is installed by editing the "env" block of ~/.claude/settings.json
 only — never a shell alias — and it is removed again on every clean exit.
 .
 GTK is a Recommends, not a Depends, so the daemon and the terminal dashboard
 still install on a headless machine (apt install --no-install-recommends). The
 top bar needs those packages; without them "tower-tray" says so and names them.
